    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch02-10: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.09";
    dc:description "The sentence is a diagnosis of why a piece of common sense fails. Engineering artifacts and natural forms can be described, and that description does not identify the psychological source of the intuition or show that the diagnosis is the reason the intuition fails. The claim has no separating measurement.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The claim explains a habit of thought by its origin in engineering practice. A survey of design methods can describe what engineers build; it cannot show that this origin is why the intuition fails, nor measure the intuition itself.";
